# Universe Civilization: Empire at Wars

> A browser-based civilization, exploration, diplomacy, and turn-based RTS war engine built for persistent worlds.

**Universe Civilization: Empire at Wars** is an open-source PHP and MariaDB strategy game project. Players develop worlds, manage infrastructure and power, command fleets, defend planets and stations, conduct covert operations, communicate with other players, and fight multi-wave battles across a procedural universe.

The project combines a preserved legacy gameplay foundation with a modern blue/cyan industrial command interface. Its architecture is intentionally modular: the PHP game shell loads feature modules through the existing AJAX contract, while database migrations provide persistent systems that can be enabled progressively.

## Current build

The current preview build includes the following playable areas:

| Area | Included systems |
|---|---|
| Civilization | Player accounts, login gate, profiles, preferences, home worlds, resources, ranks, and administration |
| Universe | Deterministic A–Z world taxonomy, planet and moon classes, biomes, sizes 1–9, intelligence profiles, and exploration data |
| Infrastructure | Construction and upgrade systems for world, moon, station, and command infrastructure |
| Power | World and orbital power nodes, production, consumption, reserve management, transfer, and recalculation operations |
| Military | Fleet catalogs, weapons, shields, armor, targeting, initiative, morale, logistics, and tactical orders |
| Battles | Turn-based RTS combat, orbital and planetary theaters, attack and defense waves, missions, events, reports, salvage, and retreat |
| Covert operations | Sabotage missions, infiltration, detection, temporary effects, counterintelligence, cooldowns, and recovery |
| Communications | Private messages, guild channels, unread tracking, safe composition, and guild membership checks |
| Operations | Administrator control plane, game tuning, maintenance jobs, audit records, and security controls |
| Presentation | Redesigned galaxy panels, logo, title-page audio, UI effects, release information, Terms of Service, and privacy pages |

## Quick start

The project requires PHP 8.3 or later with `mysqli`, MariaDB/MySQL, and a web browser. From the repository root:

```bash
# Initialize the core database when required
mysql -u root -p < database/sql/01_create_database.sql

# Import the legacy core schema
mysql -u sgw -psgwpass sgw < game.sql

# Apply migrations and feature tables
./scripts/backend/db_migrate.sh

# Run health checks
./scripts/backend/healthcheck.sh

# Start the local game server
/usr/bin/php -S 0.0.0.0:8080
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:8080/index.php`. The public title page is the entry point for player login and account creation. The administrator console is available at `/admin/` and is protected separately from player authentication.

## Account access

Player login is enabled by default. New players use **Found Your Civilization** on the title page, while returning players use **Civilization Login**. Account settings are available from the authenticated command shell.

Administrator credentials are deployment-specific and must not be committed to the repository. Configure an administrator account through the local database or deployment process, then change any development password before exposing the game publicly. See [`LOGIN_README.md`](LOGIN_README.md) for the complete access guide.

