## Architecture

The application uses PHP classes in `base/`, AJAX-loaded gameplay modules in `modules/`, HTML templates in `templates/`, browser helpers in `js/`, and ordered SQL migrations in `database/sql/`. The legacy `Game` class remains the central compatibility layer for player state, resources, technology, and turn calculations. New systems add focused modules and defensive runtime bootstraps while retaining the existing session and navigation contracts.

The server is authoritative for authentication, permissions, resources, upgrades, battle actions, sabotage, and messages. Browser controls are presentation only and must never be trusted for game-state validation.

## Quality and safety

Before submitting changes, run PHP syntax checks, the backend health check, migration validation, and any relevant test scripts:

```bash
find . -type f -name '*.php' -print0 | xargs -0 -n1 php -l
./scripts/backend/healthcheck.sh
php tests/progression_caps_test.php
 git diff --check
```

Do not commit passwords, API keys, database dumps containing personal information, session files, or production exports. Use local configuration overrides and environment variables. Public deployments should use HTTPS, restrict `/admin/`, rotate development credentials, back up MariaDB, and review audit logs.

## Project status

This is an active pre-alpha modernization project. The account, title-page, infrastructure, power, procedural universe, combat, wave, sabotage, communications, and administrator foundations are present, but some legacy modules remain partial and require continued regression testing. New features should preserve compatibility with existing data and should add migration coverage, server-side validation, and a browser smoke test.

## Credits and project link

Graphics and systems are maintained through [github.com/ArkansasIo](https://github.com/ArkansasIo). The repository is intended for collaborative development and experimentation in persistent browser strategy systems.
